++dtype allow-lists. SM89 and SM120 have FP8 tensor cores, and CuTe
++exposes warp.MmaFP8Op (m16n8k32) plus 8-bit ldmatrix atoms for them, so
++FP8 only needs those three swapped:
++
++- MmaFP8Op with a 32-element contraction step for both gemms;
++- LdMatrix8x16x8bOp / LdMatrix16x8x8bOp(transpose) for 1-byte operands,
++  so V is read from the same (tile_n, head_dim_v) smem tile as before;
++- can_implement accepts fp8, sizes smem by the real element width, and
++  requires head_dim and tile_n to be multiples of the 32-wide step.
++
++Scales stay outside the kernel: q/k descales fold into softmax_scale and
++the v descale into the output, so no descale plumbing is added here.
++P is already produced with acc_S.load().to(self.dtype), which converts
++to fp8 unchanged.
